msgid "`@pantoken/plugin-deprecations` — lifecycle-aware compatibility shims for dropped upstream tokens."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/pantoken/deprecations/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "When an upstream release drops a `--instui-*` token, a hand-authored `DeprecationLedger`\nrecords its lifecycle: when it was deprecated, the upstream minor that will remove it, and how to\nkeep it working meanwhile — either forward to a canonical token (`replacement` → `var(...)`) or\nfreeze its last-known literal (`value`). This plugin appends one shim token per entry. Because the\nshim is a single `var(...)` or a plain value, `defineToken` records its `refersTo`/syntax and\n`toCss` emits it, so the shim rides into css/scss/less/stylus/wordpress/vanilla with no extra wiring."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/pantoken/deprecations/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The retirement is enforced elsewhere (the upgrade pipeline hard-fails a bump once an entry's\n`removeIn` upstream minor is reached, forcing the entry to be retired and a consumer minor cut).\n[dueForRemoval](functions/dueForRemoval.md) is the check that powers it; [describeLifecycle](functions/describeLifecycle.md) powers the docs."
msgstr ""

