#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/NESTED_DEPS.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: NESTED\\_DEPS"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/NESTED_DEPS.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Elements whose shadow markup renders another element, so registering one requires its dependencies\ntoo: `<instui-date-time-input>` renders a `<instui-date-input>`, which renders a `<instui-calendar>`.\n[register](../functions/register.md)'s `only` filter expands through this (transitively) so a cherry-picked subset still\nworks. Keyed by base name; values are direct dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/alert.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: alert"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/alert.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-alert>` — an inline status message with `role=\"alert\"`. The `variant` attribute maps to the\n`-color-<variant>` modifier (`info`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`). Alerts are elevated by default;\nset `has-shadow=\"false\"` to flatten one (→ `-without-shadow`, mirroring InstUI's `hasShadow={false}`).\nThe `timeout` attribute (milliseconds) auto-dismisses the alert after that delay — it fades out,\nremoves itself from the DOM, and fires a cancelable bubbling `dismiss` event (call `preventDefault()`\non it to keep the alert mounted). The fade states use `@pantoken/components`' `transition` utility;\nload its stylesheet when using timeout dismissal. Slotted content is the message body."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: ar"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Arabic (العربية) locale bundle."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/avatar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: avatar"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/avatar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-avatar>` — a circular (or rectangular) avatar. `variant` maps to `-color-<variant>`,\n`size` to `-size-<size>`, and `shape=\"rectangle\"` to `-shape-rectangle`; slotted content is the\ninitials, or an `<img>` (use an absolute/CDN `src`) to show a photo."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/badge.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: badge"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/badge.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-badge>` — a small count/status badge. The `variant` attribute maps to the\n`-color-<variant>` modifier; slotted content is the count or label."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: button"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-button>` — a token-styled `<button>`. The `variant` attribute maps to the `-color-<variant>`\nmodifier (`secondary`, `tertiary`, `success`, `danger`, `ai`, …); `margin` adds spacing around the\nhost (InstUI keywords like `small` / `medium large`); slotted content is the label."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It is also a native invoker: `popovertarget` (with optional `popovertargetaction`) toggles any\nlight-DOM `[popover]` such as `<instui-context-view>`, `<instui-popover>`, or `<instui-tray>`, and\n`command`/`commandfor` drives the command-based components (`<instui-modal>` with `--show`/`--close`,\netc.). The id is forwarded to the inner button via the invoker IDL, so it resolves across the shadow\nboundary and may point forward to an element declared later in the document."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ca.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: ca"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ca.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Catalan (Catalá) locale bundle."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: calendar"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-calendar>` — an interactive month grid. `value` (`yyyy-mm-dd`) is the selected day and\n`view` (`yyyy-mm-dd`, optional) the visible month. The prev/next chevrons and every day are\n`<button>`s driving the Invoker Commands API (`--calendar-prev`, `--calendar-next`,\n`--calendar-select`) at the grid; selecting a day updates `value`/`view` and dispatches a composed,\nbubbling `change` event (`detail.value` is the ISO date). Renders its own grid (no slot), so it\nworks standalone or nested inside a date picker."
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/contextView.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:glossary"
msgid "# Variable: contextView"
msgstr ""

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/contextView.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-context-view>` — a callout surface with a caret. The host itself is a native `[popover]`\n(top layer + light-dismiss), so a light-DOM `popovertarget`/`command` button can toggle it by id.\nPosition it near its trigger with CSS anchor positioning where supported; otherwise it centres in\nthe top layer. Content goes in the default slot."
msgstr ""

